Company: ThorAI Group Location: Melbourne Title: Product Manager (The Visionary)
Our Mission: More Than Just Code, We're Building the Future. At ThorAI Group, we're not just a forward-thinking startup; we're a league of innovators on a quest to harness the power of Artificial Intelligence.
Our mission? To revolutionise industries and create solutions that redefine what's possible, think about everything from predicting the dance of binary star systems (yes, really!) to equipping the financial services industry with cutting-edge AI superpowers.
We specialise in crafting AI-driven tools that empower financial institutions to optimise operations, make super-charged decisions, and deliver client experiences that are nothing short of legendary. We're a dynamic, collaborative environment where bright minds and groundbreaking tech team up to do amazing things.
Job Summary:
We are seeking a visionary Product Manager to chart the course for our league of innovators. We need a strategic mastermind who speaks the languages of both business and technology, capable of translating bold ideas into actionable battle plans.
The ideal candidate has a passion for solving complex problems, a deep empathy for the user, and a proven history of guiding cross-functional teams to ship products that disrupt the status quo. You will be the bridge between our technical wizards and the world they serve.
Your Superpowers in Action (What You'll Conquer):
● Chart the Destiny: Define and own the product vision, strategy, and roadmap. You will act as the navigator, ensuring our AI solutions are headed toward the right galaxy.
● Translate the Mission: Gather requirements from stakeholders and customers, then translate these needs into clear, actionable user stories and specs for our engineering squads.
● Rally the League: Lead and collaborate with cross-functional squads of designers, data scientists, and developers. You are the glue that holds the alliance together, ensuring alignment and momentum.
● Master of Prescience (Data Analysis): Use data, market research, and user feedback to predict the future needs of the market. You’ll make evidence-based decisions to prioritize features that deliver maximum impact.
● Unleash the Tech: Oversee the full product lifecycle from concept to launch. You’ll ensure our releases are smooth, timely, and hit the market with the force of a meteor.
● Guardian of Value: Constantly evaluate the performance of our products, ensuring they are delivering legendary value to our financial clients and solving their most critical pain points.
Your Hero Toolkit (Required Skills & Qualifications):
● A minimum of 3-5+ years of experience in Product Management, preferably within the FinTech, SaaS, or AI sectors.
● Mastery of Agile Methodology: You know how to run sprints, stand-ups, and backlog grooming sessions like a seasoned commander.
● Tech-Savvy Intuition: You don't need to write the code, but you must understand the technical constraints and possibilities of AI and Cloud architecture (Azure knowledge is a plus).
● Communication Superpowers: You can articulate complex concepts to both technical teams and non-technical stakeholders with clarity and charisma.
● Strategic Vision: Experience building and maintaining product roadmaps using tools like Jira, Productboard, or similar.
● User-Obsessed: A track record of conducting user research and acting as the voice of the customer within the organization.
● Analytical Mindset: Proficiency in using analytics tools to measure success and iterate on the product.
Power-Ups & Perks (What We Offer):
●  A competitive salary and equity options – rewards fit for a hero, including a stake in our quest.
●  Flexible working hours and remote working options – because heroes need flexibility.
●  A collaborative, innovative, and fun work environment – your Justice League awaits!
●  Boundless opportunities for professional growth and to level up your skills.
Ready to Join the League? (How to Apply):
If you're thrilled by the chance to shape the technology of the future and make a monumental impact at ThorAI Group, send us your resume and a cover letter.
Tell us about the products you’ve launched, your greatest strategic triumphs, and why you’re the Visionary we’re looking for!


